{"id":761,"date":"2021-02-14T15:34:49","date_gmt":"2021-02-14T15:34:49","guid":{"rendered":"http:\/\/consult-ant.uk\/?p=761"},"modified":"2021-02-14T15:44:49","modified_gmt":"2021-02-14T15:44:49","slug":"diversity-in-data-feb-2021","status":"publish","type":"post","link":"https:\/\/consult-ant.uk\/2021\/02\/14\/diversity-in-data-feb-2021\/","title":{"rendered":"Diversity In Data &#8211; Feb 2021 &#8211; Web Pages and Show Hide"},"content":{"rendered":"\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">One of the three data sets for the February 2021 Diversity in Data initiative was about notable Black Scientific Achievements and Inventions.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">The data set included a field which held a wikipedia link for the associated person. When I saw this I decided I wanted to try out including a dynamic web page as part of the visualisation. And it turned out it was quite simple in the end. <\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">The final result looked like this:<\/p>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-image\"><figure class=\"aligncenter size-large\"><img data-recalc-dims=\"1\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"685\" height=\"464\" data-attachment-id=\"765\" data-permalink=\"https:\/\/consult-ant.uk\/scientificachievements\/\" data-orig-file=\"https:\/\/i0.wp.com\/consult-ant.uk\/wp-content\/uploads\/2021\/02\/scientificachievements.gif?fit=1146%2C777&amp;ssl=1\" data-orig-size=\"1146,777\" data-comments-opened=\"1\" data-image-meta=\"{&quot;aperture&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;credit&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;camera&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;caption&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;created_timestamp&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;copyright&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;focal_length&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;iso&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;shutter_speed&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;orientation&quot;:&quot;0&quot;}\" data-image-title=\"scientificachievements\" data-image-description=\"\" data-image-caption=\"\" data-large-file=\"https:\/\/i0.wp.com\/consult-ant.uk\/wp-content\/uploads\/2021\/02\/scientificachievements.gif?fit=685%2C464&amp;ssl=1\" src=\"https:\/\/i0.wp.com\/consult-ant.uk\/wp-content\/uploads\/2021\/02\/scientificachievements.gif?resize=685%2C464&#038;ssl=1\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-765\" \/><figcaption><a href=\"https:\/\/public.tableau.com\/views\/ScientificAchievementsandInventions\/BlackScientificAchievementsandInventions?:language=en-GB&amp;:display_count=y&amp;:origin=viz_share_link\">Black Scientific Achievements and Inventions<\/a><\/figcaption><\/figure><\/div>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">The background image and icons were all designed in Figma, along with the initial splash page (which sits inside a show\/hide container).<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">The animation element of moving the Light bulb\/Rosette to be next to the person title is very similar to a previous blog post I wrote (<a href=\"http:\/\/consult-ant.uk\/2020\/10\/16\/makeover-monday-week-2020-40-and-animated-hex-maps\/\">Animated Heat Maps<\/a>) and makes use of several worksheet layers.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">I&#8217;m going to focus on the <strong>Web Page<\/strong> element of this dashboard, and also touch on the <strong>Show\/Hide<\/strong> button, which I managed to make appear like it changes position to fit in the design.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><strong>Web Page<\/strong><\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">To kick this off, I first started by creating a parameter:<\/p>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-image\"><figure class=\"aligncenter size-large\"><img data-recalc-dims=\"1\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"428\" height=\"483\" data-attachment-id=\"770\" data-permalink=\"https:\/\/consult-ant.uk\/image-51\/\" data-orig-file=\"https:\/\/i0.wp.com\/consult-ant.uk\/wp-content\/uploads\/2021\/02\/image.png?fit=428%2C483&amp;ssl=1\" data-orig-size=\"428,483\" data-comments-opened=\"1\" data-image-meta=\"{&quot;aperture&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;credit&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;camera&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;caption&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;created_timestamp&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;copyright&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;focal_length&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;iso&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;shutter_speed&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;orientation&quot;:&quot;0&quot;}\" data-image-title=\"image\" data-image-description=\"\" data-image-caption=\"\" data-large-file=\"https:\/\/i0.wp.com\/consult-ant.uk\/wp-content\/uploads\/2021\/02\/image.png?fit=428%2C483&amp;ssl=1\" src=\"https:\/\/i0.wp.com\/consult-ant.uk\/wp-content\/uploads\/2021\/02\/image.png?resize=428%2C483&#038;ssl=1\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-770\" \/><\/figure><\/div>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">This will hold the specific link I want displayed in the web page. <\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Handily the data has the URL link in it for me, so I didn&#8217;t need to add these in. So in order to get these into the parameter, I just need to set up a parameter action from my chart. This is so when the user selects one of the icons the URL will change.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">To do this, I need to add the &#8216;Link&#8217; field into the detail shelf of my main chart, and then set up a parameter action on the dashboard like this:<\/p>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-image\"><figure class=\"aligncenter size-large\"><img data-recalc-dims=\"1\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"502\" height=\"532\" data-attachment-id=\"773\" data-permalink=\"https:\/\/consult-ant.uk\/image-1-7\/\" data-orig-file=\"https:\/\/i0.wp.com\/consult-ant.uk\/wp-content\/uploads\/2021\/02\/image-1.png?fit=502%2C532&amp;ssl=1\" data-orig-size=\"502,532\" data-comments-opened=\"1\" data-image-meta=\"{&quot;aperture&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;credit&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;camera&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;caption&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;created_timestamp&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;copyright&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;focal_length&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;iso&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;shutter_speed&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;orientation&quot;:&quot;0&quot;}\" data-image-title=\"image-1\" data-image-description=\"\" data-image-caption=\"\" data-large-file=\"https:\/\/i0.wp.com\/consult-ant.uk\/wp-content\/uploads\/2021\/02\/image-1.png?fit=502%2C532&amp;ssl=1\" src=\"https:\/\/i0.wp.com\/consult-ant.uk\/wp-content\/uploads\/2021\/02\/image-1.png?resize=502%2C532&#038;ssl=1\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-773\" \/><\/figure><\/div>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">This means when I click on the mark on the &#8216;Interact&#8217; sheet, the Link Parameter will be updated with the new URL.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Now this is set up, I can bring my Web Page element onto the dashboard &#8211; drag one from the Objects pane:<\/p>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-image\"><figure class=\"aligncenter size-large\"><img data-recalc-dims=\"1\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"199\" height=\"173\" data-attachment-id=\"775\" data-permalink=\"https:\/\/consult-ant.uk\/image-2-7\/\" data-orig-file=\"https:\/\/i0.wp.com\/consult-ant.uk\/wp-content\/uploads\/2021\/02\/image-2.png?fit=199%2C173&amp;ssl=1\" data-orig-size=\"199,173\" data-comments-opened=\"1\" data-image-meta=\"{&quot;aperture&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;credit&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;camera&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;caption&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;created_timestamp&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;copyright&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;focal_length&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;iso&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;shutter_speed&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;orientation&quot;:&quot;0&quot;}\" data-image-title=\"image-2\" data-image-description=\"\" data-image-caption=\"\" data-large-file=\"https:\/\/i0.wp.com\/consult-ant.uk\/wp-content\/uploads\/2021\/02\/image-2.png?fit=199%2C173&amp;ssl=1\" src=\"https:\/\/i0.wp.com\/consult-ant.uk\/wp-content\/uploads\/2021\/02\/image-2.png?resize=199%2C173&#038;ssl=1\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-775\" \/><\/figure><\/div>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">And in the &#8216;Edit URL&#8217; box, there is an arrow to the right you can click and choose what field or parameter to use in the object:<\/p>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-image\"><figure class=\"aligncenter size-large\"><img data-recalc-dims=\"1\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"685\" height=\"227\" data-attachment-id=\"779\" data-permalink=\"https:\/\/consult-ant.uk\/image-4-6\/\" data-orig-file=\"https:\/\/i0.wp.com\/consult-ant.uk\/wp-content\/uploads\/2021\/02\/image-4.png?fit=1238%2C410&amp;ssl=1\" data-orig-size=\"1238,410\" data-comments-opened=\"1\" data-image-meta=\"{&quot;aperture&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;credit&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;camera&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;caption&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;created_timestamp&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;copyright&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;focal_length&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;iso&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;shutter_speed&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;orientation&quot;:&quot;0&quot;}\" data-image-title=\"image-4\" data-image-description=\"\" data-image-caption=\"\" data-large-file=\"https:\/\/i0.wp.com\/consult-ant.uk\/wp-content\/uploads\/2021\/02\/image-4.png?fit=685%2C227&amp;ssl=1\" src=\"https:\/\/i0.wp.com\/consult-ant.uk\/wp-content\/uploads\/2021\/02\/image-4.png?resize=685%2C227&#038;ssl=1\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-779\" \/><\/figure><\/div>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Here you select &#8216;Parameters.Links Parameter&#8217; and this will be set up! Now when you select the mark on the viz, this web page object will update based on the updated parameter. Simple!<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">One issue with this data set was a lack of URLs for a couple of the people, so I had to think how to sort this out. By default if there is no URL in the parameter then it will keep with the previous web page loaded, which is a bit confusing to the user if they have selected a different mark. I decided to sort this by having a placeholder image for those URLs:<\/p>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-image\"><figure class=\"aligncenter size-large\"><img data-recalc-dims=\"1\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"423\" height=\"270\" data-attachment-id=\"780\" data-permalink=\"https:\/\/consult-ant.uk\/nowiki-1\/\" data-orig-file=\"https:\/\/i0.wp.com\/consult-ant.uk\/wp-content\/uploads\/2021\/02\/nowiki-1.png?fit=423%2C270&amp;ssl=1\" data-orig-size=\"423,270\" data-comments-opened=\"1\" data-image-meta=\"{&quot;aperture&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;credit&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;camera&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;caption&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;created_timestamp&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;copyright&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;focal_length&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;iso&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;shutter_speed&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;orientation&quot;:&quot;0&quot;}\" data-image-title=\"nowiki-1\" data-image-description=\"\" data-image-caption=\"\" data-large-file=\"https:\/\/i0.wp.com\/consult-ant.uk\/wp-content\/uploads\/2021\/02\/nowiki-1.png?fit=423%2C270&amp;ssl=1\" src=\"https:\/\/i0.wp.com\/consult-ant.uk\/wp-content\/uploads\/2021\/02\/nowiki-1.png?resize=423%2C270&#038;ssl=1\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-780\" \/><\/figure><\/div>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">I decided I would host this image on this blog site, so I can then use the URL from this site to add to my list of URLs in the data &#8211; meaning that this image would show via the Web Page when those without a wikipedia page were clicked. I also used this default image for when the user first loads the dashboard and no person is selected.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">So that was it for the Web Page part &#8211; this turned out really simple to get a dynamic web page opening on the dashboard!<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><strong>Show\/Hide Button<\/strong><\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">The other quick tip I wanted to share was around the show\/hide container button. In my dashboard, the &#8216;Splash&#8217; screen when you open the dashboard looks like this:<\/p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-large\"><img data-recalc-dims=\"1\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"685\" height=\"457\" data-attachment-id=\"762\" data-permalink=\"https:\/\/consult-ant.uk\/2021\/02\/14\/diversity-in-data-feb-2021\/black-scientific-achievements-and-inventions1\/\" data-orig-file=\"https:\/\/i0.wp.com\/consult-ant.uk\/wp-content\/uploads\/2021\/02\/black-scientific-achievements-and-inventions1.png?fit=1200%2C800&amp;ssl=1\" data-orig-size=\"1200,800\" data-comments-opened=\"1\" data-image-meta=\"{&quot;aperture&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;credit&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;camera&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;caption&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;created_timestamp&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;copyright&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;focal_length&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;iso&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;shutter_speed&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;orientation&quot;:&quot;0&quot;}\" data-image-title=\"Black Scientific Achievements and Inventions1\" data-image-description=\"\" data-image-caption=\"\" data-large-file=\"https:\/\/i0.wp.com\/consult-ant.uk\/wp-content\/uploads\/2021\/02\/black-scientific-achievements-and-inventions1.png?fit=685%2C457&amp;ssl=1\" src=\"https:\/\/i0.wp.com\/consult-ant.uk\/wp-content\/uploads\/2021\/02\/black-scientific-achievements-and-inventions1.png?resize=685%2C457&#038;ssl=1\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-762\" \/><\/figure>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">This is an open Show\/Hide container, with the close button in the top right. When this is closed the dashboard looks like this:<\/p>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-image\"><figure class=\"aligncenter size-large\"><img data-recalc-dims=\"1\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"685\" height=\"460\" data-attachment-id=\"786\" data-permalink=\"https:\/\/consult-ant.uk\/black-scientific-achievements-and-inventions2\/\" data-orig-file=\"https:\/\/i0.wp.com\/consult-ant.uk\/wp-content\/uploads\/2021\/02\/black-scientific-achievements-and-inventions2.png?fit=1145%2C769&amp;ssl=1\" data-orig-size=\"1145,769\" data-comments-opened=\"1\" data-image-meta=\"{&quot;aperture&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;credit&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;camera&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;caption&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;created_timestamp&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;copyright&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;focal_length&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;iso&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;shutter_speed&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;orientation&quot;:&quot;0&quot;}\" data-image-title=\"black-scientific-achievements-and-inventions2\" data-image-description=\"\" data-image-caption=\"\" data-large-file=\"https:\/\/i0.wp.com\/consult-ant.uk\/wp-content\/uploads\/2021\/02\/black-scientific-achievements-and-inventions2.png?fit=685%2C460&amp;ssl=1\" src=\"https:\/\/i0.wp.com\/consult-ant.uk\/wp-content\/uploads\/2021\/02\/black-scientific-achievements-and-inventions2.png?resize=685%2C460&#038;ssl=1\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-786\" \/><\/figure><\/div>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Here you can see the show\/hide button is in the top right of the pink box, but this is actually lower than the button was in the first image. I did this to fit in with the design, but how did I do it?<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Again &#8211; quite simple. This involved making the Show\/Hide button an &#8216;Image&#8217; and creating two icons in Figma (an x and an i) which are actually part of a larger rectangle (which is transparent) &#8211; the x and i are then offset to to the top and bottom of the same sized rectangle giving the illusion that the button moves. Steps below:<\/p>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-image\"><figure class=\"aligncenter size-large\"><img data-recalc-dims=\"1\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"402\" height=\"186\" data-attachment-id=\"788\" data-permalink=\"https:\/\/consult-ant.uk\/image-5-6\/\" data-orig-file=\"https:\/\/i0.wp.com\/consult-ant.uk\/wp-content\/uploads\/2021\/02\/image-5.png?fit=402%2C186&amp;ssl=1\" data-orig-size=\"402,186\" data-comments-opened=\"1\" data-image-meta=\"{&quot;aperture&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;credit&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;camera&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;caption&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;created_timestamp&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;copyright&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;focal_length&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;iso&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;shutter_speed&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;orientation&quot;:&quot;0&quot;}\" data-image-title=\"image-5\" data-image-description=\"\" data-image-caption=\"\" data-large-file=\"https:\/\/i0.wp.com\/consult-ant.uk\/wp-content\/uploads\/2021\/02\/image-5.png?fit=402%2C186&amp;ssl=1\" src=\"https:\/\/i0.wp.com\/consult-ant.uk\/wp-content\/uploads\/2021\/02\/image-5.png?resize=402%2C186&#038;ssl=1\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-788\" \/><figcaption>Make a container a &#8216;Show Hide&#8217; container<\/figcaption><\/figure><\/div>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-jetpack-layout-grid alignfull column1-desktop-grid__span-1 column1-desktop-grid__start-6 column1-desktop-grid__row-1 column2-desktop-grid__span-1 column2-desktop-grid__start-7 column2-desktop-grid__row-1 column1-tablet-grid__span-4 column1-tablet-grid__row-1 column2-tablet-grid__span-4 column2-tablet-grid__start-5 column2-tablet-grid__row-1 column1-mobile-grid__span-4 column1-mobile-grid__row-1 column2-mobile-grid__span-4 column2-mobile-grid__row-2 wp-block-jetpack-layout-gutter__huge\">\n<div class=\"wp-block-jetpack-layout-grid-column wp-block-jetpack-layout-grid__padding-none\">\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-large\"><img data-recalc-dims=\"1\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"60\" height=\"93\" data-attachment-id=\"791\" data-permalink=\"https:\/\/consult-ant.uk\/xoffset\/\" data-orig-file=\"https:\/\/i0.wp.com\/consult-ant.uk\/wp-content\/uploads\/2021\/02\/xoffset.png?fit=60%2C93&amp;ssl=1\" data-orig-size=\"60,93\" data-comments-opened=\"1\" data-image-meta=\"{&quot;aperture&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;credit&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;camera&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;caption&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;created_timestamp&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;copyright&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;focal_length&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;iso&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;shutter_speed&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;orientation&quot;:&quot;0&quot;}\" data-image-title=\"xoffset\" data-image-description=\"\" data-image-caption=\"\" data-large-file=\"https:\/\/i0.wp.com\/consult-ant.uk\/wp-content\/uploads\/2021\/02\/xoffset.png?fit=60%2C93&amp;ssl=1\" src=\"https:\/\/i0.wp.com\/consult-ant.uk\/wp-content\/uploads\/2021\/02\/xoffset.png?resize=60%2C93&#038;ssl=1\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-791\" \/><\/figure>\n<\/div>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-jetpack-layout-grid-column wp-block-jetpack-layout-grid__padding-none\">\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-large\"><img data-recalc-dims=\"1\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"60\" height=\"89\" data-attachment-id=\"790\" data-permalink=\"https:\/\/consult-ant.uk\/ioffset\/\" data-orig-file=\"https:\/\/i0.wp.com\/consult-ant.uk\/wp-content\/uploads\/2021\/02\/ioffset.png?fit=60%2C89&amp;ssl=1\" data-orig-size=\"60,89\" data-comments-opened=\"1\" data-image-meta=\"{&quot;aperture&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;credit&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;camera&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;caption&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;created_timestamp&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;copyright&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;focal_length&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;iso&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;shutter_speed&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;orientation&quot;:&quot;0&quot;}\" data-image-title=\"ioffset\" data-image-description=\"\" data-image-caption=\"\" data-large-file=\"https:\/\/i0.wp.com\/consult-ant.uk\/wp-content\/uploads\/2021\/02\/ioffset.png?fit=60%2C89&amp;ssl=1\" src=\"https:\/\/i0.wp.com\/consult-ant.uk\/wp-content\/uploads\/2021\/02\/ioffset.png?resize=60%2C89&#038;ssl=1\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-790\" \/><\/figure>\n<\/div>\n<\/div>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"has-text-align-center wp-block-paragraph\"><em>Show\/Hide button images<\/em><\/p>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-image\"><figure class=\"aligncenter size-large\"><img data-recalc-dims=\"1\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"409\" height=\"559\" data-attachment-id=\"794\" data-permalink=\"https:\/\/consult-ant.uk\/image-6-6\/\" data-orig-file=\"https:\/\/i0.wp.com\/consult-ant.uk\/wp-content\/uploads\/2021\/02\/image-6.png?fit=409%2C559&amp;ssl=1\" data-orig-size=\"409,559\" data-comments-opened=\"1\" data-image-meta=\"{&quot;aperture&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;credit&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;camera&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;caption&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;created_timestamp&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;copyright&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;focal_length&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;iso&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;shutter_speed&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;orientation&quot;:&quot;0&quot;}\" data-image-title=\"image-6\" data-image-description=\"\" data-image-caption=\"\" data-large-file=\"https:\/\/i0.wp.com\/consult-ant.uk\/wp-content\/uploads\/2021\/02\/image-6.png?fit=409%2C559&amp;ssl=1\" src=\"https:\/\/i0.wp.com\/consult-ant.uk\/wp-content\/uploads\/2021\/02\/image-6.png?resize=409%2C559&#038;ssl=1\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-794\" \/><figcaption>Show\/Hide Button Settings<\/figcaption><\/figure><\/div>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-image\"><figure class=\"aligncenter size-large\"><img data-recalc-dims=\"1\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"173\" height=\"171\" data-attachment-id=\"796\" data-permalink=\"https:\/\/consult-ant.uk\/image-7-5\/\" data-orig-file=\"https:\/\/i0.wp.com\/consult-ant.uk\/wp-content\/uploads\/2021\/02\/image-7.png?fit=173%2C171&amp